hey Guardians the destiny to beta is now  available for all to shoot and loot  their way through the game's opening  story mission a strike and some hot PvP  while the beta might not be quite as  extensive as the one for the original  destiny there is still a lot we were  able to learn from our time with it if  you end up enjoying this video make sure  to give us a like and sub because we're  sure to have plenty more destiny content  down the road before the game launches  [Music]  Oh  [Music]  shaders in the original destiny were a  great way to make your guardian feel  unique but they were limited to presets  and you couldn't get crazy with the  customization poking around in destiny  two's menus you can now see that shaders  can be applied to individual pieces of  armor and not just armor but also  weapons your ghosts and even your ship  exotics seem to be the exception maybe  because Bungie still plans on using the  ornament system that was added in Rise  of iron in addition to changing the look  of your gun you can also customize  certain weapons both energy and power  weapons have mod slots meaning you can  swap a solar mod for an ark mod that  fits their play style this opens up a  lot of possibilities and saves some  headache where in destiny 1 you would  need a certain damage type but it  happened to be on a gun you didn't like  now you can just swap around and you're  good  the beta strike the inverted spire is  actually pretty open-ended at the  beginning with a decent amount of  explorable space to it  considering how a lot of strikes in the  first destiny would start in the free  roam areas before leading to a strike  specific location this is probably true  for the inverted spire this means you  get a taste of what the patrol area for  the planet of necess will be like it's  pretty empty though in its current beta  form so don't expect to find much but  some smart destiny players have already  glitched their way through some  unfinished areas we clearly weren't  meant to find  [Music]  in the beta you get access to all three  classes there are old subclasses with  some changes and new subclasses perhaps  the biggest overall change for the  classes is a new third universal ability  that each class has regardless of their  subclass the Titan gets the brand new  Sentinel subclass with the ability to  form a void shield and throw it at  people like Captain America and at  ricochets you start with only one throw  but can upgrade it to two and if you  happen to miss the bubble from destiny  ones defender class don't worry you can  still make one the strikers fists of  havoc is pretty similar but you can now  shoulder charge enemies while your super  is active the Titans Universal ability  either lets them create a large barrier  to protect themselves or a small barrier  that when taking cover behind reloads  their weapon  since Destiny's reveal we've already  seen a good amount of the Warlocks new  class the dawn blade which lets you  float in the air and throw blades of  light at people a fun trick we learned  is that you can do a mid-air dodge  similar to be Twilight garrison exotic  chess piece in d1 which was originally  only for Titans the void Walker class  has a small change with its super the  nova bomb which now tracks enemies and  will send out a little accion bolts when  it lands the warlocks new universal  ability lets them create a field that  will heal both themselves and teammates  the hunters new arc starter class is a  replacement for the Blade Dancer and  it's super serves a similar function but  now has a bit more range to it the  changes are a little more  behind-the-scenes though where by  combining it with your dodge ability you  can choose to either keep your combo  going longer or dish out more damage  this gives the arc staff more variety in  how to use it the gunslingers big change  is that fast players can now shoot up to  6 times with the Golden Gun  instead of the normal three and you can  upgrade it for even more shots if you  get a precision hit the universal  ability for the hunter is a McCree style  dodge roll which you can either reload  your weapon with or recharge your melee  those are a few of the things we found  while playing destiny choose beta if you  found anything cool debated that excites  you throw it in those comments we also  have plenty of awesome gameplay if  you're interested so be sure to check  that out thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

